  "reviewNotes": "All 8 native archives reviewed with scripts/review_final.py (release pipeline first-layer parser). Every object has a positive flat model first layer equal (to 0.01 mm2) to the file already being printed, so each part sits on its adopted face: Yellow head_bottom lying flat 1297/1298 mm2; Orange head_cap lying flat 451 mm2; White face_panel 3021/3023 mm2; Black 7 objects including openrb_tray 2238/2240 mm2. Object counts match the printing files (Y1, W1, O4, B7); all-layer extrusion footprints inside the bed. Support blockers present as nonprinting modifiers; support extrusion inside each blocker region and both OpenRB tray lip slots is equal to the file being printed (tray lip slots and Pi/pilot hole cores: zero). Prepared projects are byte-identical to the per-colour runs; command-stream differences against the printing files are recorded in ../stream-diff.json."
